Z||000000||AutoXer||07-31-2001||01:22 PM||||Have any of you guys had a problem with your deck lid bolts getting stripped out?<P>What did you do about it?<P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||07-31-2001||05:02 PM||||I just ran a SAE tap into the stripped out hole and a put in a bolt from the hardware store, sorry but I don't remember the size.||||reg||1
Z||000002||qwikgta||07-31-2001||11:25 PM||||My understanding is that there is an epoxyed in nut on the other side that if it brakes loose will feel like it is stripped.  Im not sure if this is what your are talking about.  In my case a bolt would not get tight and after a while it would just come right off (not in the treads), A friend in my local club told me about the nut thing.  If it is true it make sence to me.  My only fix is to drill a hole through the other side and put in a 3" bolt all the way through the deck lid.<P><BR>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject   <BR>http://www.vafieros.com<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
